# Rust Language Support

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:lux, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "../..")}
])
```

## Overview

Lux provides native Rust support for high-throughput computational kernels, cryptographic routines, and vector operations.

## Basic Usage

```elixir
require Lux.Rust
import Lux.Rust

# Execute native function
{:ok, result} = Lux.Rust.call("math.fibonacci", %{"n" => 20})
IO.puts("Fibonacci(20) = #{result}")
```

## Using the `~RS` Sigil

```elixir
rust variables: %{x: 40, y: 2} do
  ~RS"""
  pub fn main(args: Map) -> i64 {
      args["x"] + args["y"]
  }
  """
end
```
